# Everything is stored and checked out with LF, whatever the contributor's platform.
# The .editorconfig states the same rule for editors; this states it for git, so a Windows
# checkout cannot commit CRLF by accident. Binary files are detected and left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Tooling that writes CRLF regardless: "dotnet sln add" rewrites the solution file with a
# UTF-8 BOM and CRLF endings every time a project is added. Git normalises the endings here;
# the BOM is caught by the ASCII check in CI (see .github/workflows/ci.yml).
*.sln text eol=lf

# Vendored conformance packages are compressed archives: never touch their bytes. Their
# digests are recorded in profiles/packages/manifest.json and verified in CI.
*.tgz binary
*.zip binary
